E8539 Route `order` takes an `access_token` and opens nothing through a door
  --> controllers_link.py:11:5
   |
 9 | class Portal(http.Controller):
10 |     @http.route("/my/order/<int:order_id>", type="http", auth="public")
11 |     def order(self, order_id, access_token=None):  # E8539
   |     ^^^^^^^^^
12 |         order = request.env["sale.order"].browse(order_id)
13 |         if order.access_token != access_token:
   |
help: Declare `auth="link"`, or reach a door such as `_open_record`

